winex11: glx_renderer only exists when GLX does.

X11DRV_HasWindowManager() answers "xwayland_glx_nvidia" by reading
`glx_renderer`, which x11drv.h declares unconditionally and opengl.c defines
inside `#ifdef SONAME_LIBGL`. Configure the tree without libGL and the reference
has nothing to bind to:

    ld.lld: error: undefined symbol: glx_renderer
    make: *** [dlls/winex11.drv/winex11.so] Error 1

after every object has compiled, which is a long way to go to find a missing
`#ifdef`.

This is Valve's code -- upstream Wine 11.14's window.c has no reference to
glx_renderer at all -- and a Proton build on a desktop always has libGL, so
nothing there ever hits it.

The Android build never can. There is no GLX: Vessel drives Vulkan directly and
ships Zink as a native opengl32.dll, so build/wine.sh configures GLX out and
SONAME_LIBGL is undefined.

Returning FALSE is not a stub, it is the correct answer. The query asks whether
the host is XWayland running on NVIDIA's GLX driver, which is a workaround for
one desktop configuration; Vessel's X server is neither. The other branch of the
same function, the plain "xwayland" query, needs no guard and keeps working.
diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
index cc0538d511..ab65dab339 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -4150,9 +4150,27 @@ BOOL X11DRV_HasWindowManager( const char *name )
     int opcode, event, error;
 
     if (!strcmp( name, "xwayland" )) return XQueryExtension( gdi_display, "XWAYLAND", &opcode, &event, &error );
+#ifdef SONAME_LIBGL
     if (!strcmp( name, "xwayland_glx_nvidia" ))
         return XQueryExtension( gdi_display, "XWAYLAND", &opcode, &event, &error ) && glx_renderer
                && strstr( glx_renderer, "NVIDIA" );
+#else
+    /* VESSEL: glx_renderer only exists when GLX does.
+     *
+     * It is declared in x11drv.h unconditionally but defined in opengl.c inside
+     * `#ifdef SONAME_LIBGL`, so on a build configured without libGL this
+     * reference has no definition to bind to and winex11.so fails to link:
+     *     ld.lld: error: undefined symbol: glx_renderer
+     * The Android build is exactly that build -- there is no GLX, Vessel drives
+     * Vulkan directly and ships Zink as opengl32.dll.
+     *
+     * The answer is FALSE rather than a stub renderer string, and it is the
+     * true answer: this asks "is the host XWayland running on the NVIDIA GLX
+     * driver", a Valve workaround for a desktop configuration. Vessel's X server
+     * is neither XWayland nor NVIDIA.
+     */
+    if (!strcmp( name, "xwayland_glx_nvidia" )) return FALSE;
+#endif
     return data->window_manager && !strcmp( data->window_manager, name );
 }
 
